# 低频词汇 List10
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List10核心词汇

{{decay}}{/dɪˈkeɪ/}{腐烂；衰退}{The old building fell into decay after years of neglect.}}
{{deceive}}{/dɪˈsiːv/}{欺骗；蒙蔽}{The company tried to deceive customers with false advertising.}}
{{decisive}}{/dɪˈsaɪsɪv/}{决定性的；果断的}{The general made a decisive move that won the battle.}}
{{declaration}}{/ˌdekləˈreɪʃn/}{宣言；声明}{The declaration of independence was signed in 1776.}}
{{decline}}{/dɪˈklaɪn/}{下降；谢绝}{She politely declined the invitation to the party.}}
{{dedicate}}{/ˈdedɪkeɪt/}{致力于；奉献}{He dedicated his life to protecting the environment.}}
{{deduce}}{/dɪˈdjuːs/}{推断；演绎}{From the evidence, we can deduce that the theory is correct.}}
{{deem}}{/diːm/}{认为；视为}{The court deemed the evidence insufficient.}}
{{default}}{/dɪˈfɔːlt/}{默认；违约}{The bank threatened to take action in case of default.}}
{{deficiency}}{/dɪˈfɪʃnsi/}{缺乏；不足}{A vitamin D deficiency can lead to bone problems.}}
{{deficit}}{/ˈdefɪsɪt/}{赤字；亏损}{The government is working to reduce the budget deficit.}}
{{defy}}{/dɪˈfaɪ/}{违抗；蔑视}{The activists defied the ban and held a peaceful protest.}}
{{delegate}}{/ˈdelɪɡeɪt/}{委托；代表}{A good manager knows how to delegate tasks effectively.}}
{{deliberate}}{/dɪˈlɪbərət/}{故意的；审议的}{The committee took deliberate action to address the issue.}}
{{democracy}}{/dɪˈmɒkrəsi/}{民主；民主制度}{Freedom of speech is a pillar of democracy.}}
{{demographic}}{/ˌdeməˈɡræfɪk/}{人口统计的}{The demographic shift is changing the country's workforce.}}
{{denounce}}{/dɪˈnaʊns/}{谴责；告发}{The organization denounced the use of chemical weapons.}}
{{dense}}{/dens/}{密集的；浓密的}{The forest is so dense that sunlight barely reaches the ground.}}
{{depict}}{/dɪˈpɪkt/}{描绘；描写}{The mural depicts scenes from the country's history.}}
{{deploy}}{/dɪˈplɔɪ/}{部署；使用}{The company deployed new security measures across all offices.}}
{{depression}}{/dɪˈpreʃn/}{沮丧；萧条}{The Great Depression of the 1930s affected millions worldwide.}}
{{deprive}}{/dɪˈpraɪv/}{剥夺；使丧失}{The sanctions deprived the country of essential goods.}}
{{descend}}{/dɪˈsend/}{下降；遗传}{The plane began to descend as it approached the airport.}}
{{designate}}{/ˈdezɪɡneɪt/}{指定；命名}{The area was designated as a national park.}}
{{despair}}{/dɪˈspeər/}{绝望；失望}{The refugees were filled with despair after months of hardship.}}
{{destiny}}{/ˈdestɪni/}{命运；天命}{She believed it was her destiny to become a doctor.}}
{{detach}}{/dɪˈtætʃ/}{分离；拆开}{The label can be easily detached from the package.}}
{{detain}}{/dɪˈteɪn/}{拘留；扣留}{The police detained the suspect for questioning.}}
{{deteriorate}}{/dɪˈtɪəriəreɪt/}{恶化；退化}{His health deteriorated rapidly after the diagnosis.}}
{{devastate}}{/ˈdevəsteɪt/}{毁灭；摧毁}{The hurricane devastated the coastal community.}}
